From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Keep GDI drawn into child windows that have a pixel format.

With PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1, GTA III, Vice City and San Andreas looked
minimized while their intro videos played (#958): the fullscreen window
showed the desktop behind it, then came back black between the videos.

The intros play through DirectShow. VMR7 makes its video window a child
of the game window and draws each frame with DirectDraw's windowed
primary, which gives the video window a pixel format but copies the
frames with GDI. The video window then counts as self-presenting, so
its whole area is cut out of the game window's surface, and the GDI
frames that land there are thrown away. Its own client surface never
presents, so the window is transparent.

Same-window GDI over a native frame is already kept (self-painted
region) until the window presents again. Apply that to child windows
with a pixel format too, not only to the toplevel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/dce.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/dce.c
@@ -1662,7 +1662,12 @@
 
         if (!foreign)
         {
-            if (dce->hwnd == top_win && !user_driver->dc_funcs.pPutImage &&
+            /* GDI drawn into a window that has its own client surface is newer
+             * than that window's native frame, until it presents again. This
+             * includes child windows: DirectDraw's windowed primary (used by
+             * the DirectShow VMR7, as in GTA III's intro videos) gives the
+             * video window a pixel format but copies its frames with GDI. */
+            if (!user_driver->dc_funcs.pPutImage &&
                 (paint_flags & (SET_WINPOS_PIXEL_FORMAT | SET_WINPOS_CLIP_CLIENT)))
                 source = SURFACE_GDI_OVER_SELF;
             else if (dce->hwnd != top_win &&
